    <GaugingStation location="Cyff flume" name="Cyff" number="55034">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume. Long term IH/UKCEH research catchment. Natural flow regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Shoal formation common, requiring prompt removal to avoid drowning. Check gauged by c/m, and volumetrically at lowest flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume designed by Hydraulics Research Ltd, suitable for streams with steep gradients, heavy sediment loads and high flood/drought flow ratios. Catchment nested within Cefn Brwyn (55008). Primary 15 minute dataset available.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Daily mean flows replaced from 01/10/1973 to 31/12/2010, and AMAX flows from 01/10/1973 to 01/10/2010 following detailed QC (August 2025, WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Responsive flow regime. Natural to within 10% at Q95.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Very wet catchment; drains Plynlimon massif. Composed of Ordovician grits, shales and slates and Silurian mudstones, mostly covered by peaty soils. Mainly natural or partly reseeded grassland, supporting sheep grazing.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
